on't  care if it's a citizen said that there's  a secret investigation going on or it's  a police officer people need to be  treated fairly and on four  police officers are not treated fairly  so so you think it's the accusation  against a police officer they're  presumed guilty by the community so  there's a distrust between the community  police police don't trust the accusation  no or no no it is the investigative body  all cases that involve shootings are  sent to the to the federal to the FBI  and to the state's attorney's office for  prosecution I think what we're getting  at and it's painfully obvious when you  have a thousand detective deaths deficit  on a police force it could be a lot of  things is it is it money not allocated  is it the pay is not enough is it  demoralize police is it too dangerous  and people feel like for the risk I'm  taking I'm not getting much of a benefit  you're damned if you do you're damned if  you don't why am I gonna do this job me  police policing should be it is a noble  profession but Anthony it's you here two  police officers they feel like  oftentimes they feel like they can do no  right but we have concerned citizens who  say we need more of a collaboration here  well I've gotta be able to fix this I'd  love to answer that question I was a  police officer myself I worked the  street I worked in the 15 district in  Austin I was a gang enforcement officer  so to answer this young lady's question  I've done that job I built relationships  on the street with other officers and  there was the ability to work crime  based off relationships you have but  what's happened is a culture through  America now as the police are becoming  enemy the neighborhoods are kind of  closing their doors and don't want to  answer the police don't be a snitch  don't be a snitch cuz snitch kids and  snitches get stitches and that's a  concept on the street I've seen that  t-shirt yeah and you know what there's  always this concept that there's this